body:
## Contexto
SAP delivers standard Fiori apps. Customization sin modificar el source SAP:
- Extensibility API (recommended)
- Component extension (older)
- Deep customization (avoid)

## Extension project
BAS wizard → **Extension project → Fiori extension**.

Select base app → BAS creates extension project que overrides specific parts.

## Types of extension

### View extension
Add sections, buttons, columns a existing view sin modificar original.

```xml
<!-- MyExtension.fragment.xml -->
<core:FragmentDefinition xmlns='sap.m' xmlns:core='sap.ui.core'>
    <Text text='Custom info'/>
</core:FragmentDefinition>
```

Register en extension config → gets injected en 'ExtensionPoint' declared en base view.

### Controller extension
Override controller methods:

```javascript
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/core/mvc/ControllerExtension'
], function(ControllerExtension) {
    return ControllerExtension.extend('com.empresa.ext.MyExtension', {
        override: {
            onInit: function() {
                // Custom initialization
            },
            onSavePress: function() {
                // Custom save logic
                this.base.onSavePress.apply(this, arguments);  // Call original
            }
        }
    });
});
```

### View replacement
Replace entire view con custom implementation. Rare — usually last resort.

### i18n extension
Add/override texts:
```properties
# extension/i18n/i18n.properties
customTitle=Mi Título Personalizado
```

## Register extension
Component.js del extension:
```javascript
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/core/UIComponent'
], function(UIComponent) {
    return UIComponent.extend('com.empresa.ext.Component', {
        metadata: {
            manifest: 'json',
            extends: {
                extensions: {
                    'sap.ui.viewExtensions': {
                        'sap.suite.ui.generic.template.ListReport.view.ListReport': {
                            'ListReportExt': {
                                type: 'XML',
                                fragmentName: 'com.empresa.ext.view.MyExtension'
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    'sap.ui.controllerExtensions': {
                        'sap.suite.ui.generic.template.ListReport.view.ListReport': {
                            controllerName: 'com.empresa.ext.controller.ListReportExt'
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    });
});
```

## Deploy extension
Extension is standalone app. Deploy as usual (MTA, ABAP repo).

Runtime: extension component loads on top of standard app.

## Manifest changes
### Base app manifest.appConfig
Original app manifest is not modified.

### Extension manifest
Extension manifest declares extension points + overrides.

## Fiori launchpad tile
- Tile can point to extension component
- Or use original tile (extension auto-detected)

## Testing
1. Access original app URL → verify still works
2. Access via launchpad tile with extension → verify customizations visible

## Best practices
- **Minimize extension footprint** — only what's needed
- **Version tracking** — extensions con base app version
- **Regression testing** después SAP updates

## Runtime authoring (RTA)
Usuarios finales pueden extender via RTA (drag/drop editing):
- Adapt UI mode
- Save personalizations
- Distinguish user personalization vs developer extension

## Common issues
- **Extension not loading** — component ID mismatch
- **Override not applied** — method name typo
- **Broken after SAP update** — base view structure changed, adjust extension

## Application lifecycle

### 1. Load
- sap-ui-core.js loaded
- Component created (Component.js)
- Manifest.json parsed
- Dependencies loaded

### 2. Component init
```javascript
init: function() {
    UIComponent.prototype.init.apply(this, arguments);
    this.getRouter().initialize();
}
```

### 3. Router
- Route matched based on URL hash
- Target view loaded

### 4. View lifecycle
```javascript
onBeforeRendering: function() {
    // Before DOM insert
},
onAfterRendering: function() {
    // After DOM ready — safe to query DOM
},
onExit: function() {
    // View destroyed — cleanup
}
```

### 5. Controller lifecycle
```javascript
onInit: function() {
    // First initialization
    this._loadData();
},
onExit: function() {
    // Cleanup timers, subscribers
    clearInterval(this._timer);
}
```

## Component-level events

### Init
```javascript
init: function() {
    // Set up global services, models
    this.setModel(new JSONModel({}));
}
```

### Destroy
```javascript
destroy: function() {
    // Cleanup services
    UIComponent.prototype.destroy.apply(this, arguments);
}
```

## Route-level events
```javascript
// In Component or controller
this.getRouter().attachRoutePatternMatched(function(oEvent) {
    var sName = oEvent.getParameter('name');
    var oArgs = oEvent.getParameter('arguments');
    // React to route change
});

this.getRouter().attachBypassed(function(oEvent) {
    // Route not matched (fallback)
});
```

## Model events
```javascript
oModel.attachRequestSent((oEvent) => {
    // Before OData request
});

oModel.attachRequestCompleted((oEvent) => {
    // After OData response
});

oModel.attachRequestFailed((oEvent) => {
    // Error
});

oModel.attachPropertyChange((oEvent) => {
    // Model property changed
});
```

## Application-level
```javascript
sap.ui.getCore().attachInit(function() {
    // Core initialized
});

window.addEventListener('beforeunload', function(e) {
    // Before user leaves
    if (oModel.hasPendingChanges()) {
        e.preventDefault();
        return 'Unsaved changes!';
    }
});
```

## Navigation events
```javascript
this.getOwnerComponent().getRouter().attachRouteMatched((oEvent) => {
    var name = oEvent.getParameter('name');
});

// User back button
sap.ui.core.routing.History.getInstance().attachHistoryChanged((oEvent) => {
    // History changed
});
```

## Async patterns
```javascript
onInit: async function() {
    try {
        await this._loadData();
        await this._loadPreferences();
        this._render();
    } catch (err) {
        MessageBox.error('Load failed: ' + err.message);
    }
}
```

## Error handling globally
```javascript
sap.ui.getCore().attachError(function(oEvent) {
    // Uncaught error
    console.error('UI5 error:', oEvent.getParameters());
});

window.onerror = function(msg, src, line, col, err) {
    // Browser-level error
    logToServer({ msg, src, line, err });
};
```

## Memory management
```javascript
onExit: function() {
    // Destroy dialogs to prevent leak
    if (this._oDialog) {
        this._oDialog.destroy();
        this._oDialog = null;
    }

    // Clear timers
    clearInterval(this._timer);

    // Unsubscribe events
    this._subscription.destroy();
}
```

Otherwise: memory leaks accumulate over long sessions.

## Debug lifecycle
Enable UI5 log level trace:
```
?sap-ui-log-level=TRACE
```

Console floods with lifecycle events.

## Best practices
- **Init once, destroy once** — no side effects duplicate
- **Cleanup in onExit** — timers, listeners, subscriptions
- **Async safely** — handle errors
- **onInit for setup**, not `onBeforeRendering`
- **Store dialog refs** as controller properties to avoid recreation

## UploadCollection (recomendado)
Más rich UX. Preview, progress, drag/drop.

### View
```xml
<UploadCollection id='uploadCollection'
    uploadUrl='/api/upload'
    change='.onFileChange'
    uploadComplete='.onUploadComplete'
    beforeUploadStarts='.onBeforeUpload'
    maximumFilenameLength='60'
    maximumFileSize='10'
    fileType='pdf,jpg,png,docx'
    multiple='true'/>
```

### Controller
```javascript
onBeforeUpload: function(oEvent) {
    // Add auth headers
    var oCustomerHeaderToken = new sap.m.UploadCollectionParameter({
        name: 'x-csrf-token',
        value: this._csrfToken
    });
    oEvent.getParameters().addHeaderParameter(oCustomerHeaderToken);
},

onUploadComplete: function(oEvent) {
    var oParams = oEvent.getParameters();
    if (oParams.status === 200 || oParams.status === 201) {
        MessageToast.show('Upload OK');
        this._refreshList();
    } else {
        MessageBox.error('Upload failed: ' + oParams.responseRaw);
    }
},

onFileChange: function(oEvent) {
    // Validate before upload
    var files = oEvent.getParameters().files;
    for (var i = 0; i < files.length; i++) {
        if (files[i].size > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {
            MessageBox.error('File too large (max 10MB)');
            return;
        }
    }
}
```

## FileUploader (simpler)
```xml
<u:FileUploader xmlns:u='sap.ui.unified'
    uploadUrl='/api/upload'
    typeMissmatch='.onTypeMismatch'
    change='.onFileSelected'
    uploadComplete='.onUploadComplete'
    fileType='pdf,docx'
    maximumFileSize='10'/>
```

## OData with attachments (media entities)
Backend OData con `HasStream=true`:
```xml
<EntitySet Name='Attachments' EntityType='...' HasStream='true'/>
```

Upload via POST binary to `/Attachments`.

Download: GET `/Attachments(1)/$value`.

## Multipart upload for large files
Split large file → upload chunks → assemble server-side.

```javascript
async function uploadChunked(file) {
    const chunkSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024;  // 5 MB
    for (let start = 0; start < file.size; start += chunkSize) {
        const chunk = file.slice(start, start + chunkSize);
        await fetch('/api/upload-chunk', {
            method: 'POST',
            body: chunk,
            headers: { 'X-Range': `${start}-${start+chunk.size}/${file.size}` }
        });
    }
}
```

## Progress indicator
```javascript
var xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
xhr.upload.addEventListener('progress', function(e) {
    var percent = (e.loaded / e.total) * 100;
    oProgressBar.setPercentValue(percent);
});
xhr.open('POST', '/api/upload');
xhr.send(file);
```

## CSRF token
GET request first to fetch token:
```javascript
fetch('/api/csrf', {
    method: 'GET',
    headers: { 'X-CSRF-Token': 'Fetch' }
}).then(r => {
    this._csrfToken = r.headers.get('X-CSRF-Token');
});
```

Include en subsequent POST.

## Drag-and-drop
UploadCollection supports drag-drop natively.

For freestyle:
```javascript
droparea.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    var files = e.dataTransfer.files;
    // Upload files
});
```

## Common issues

### CORS blocked
Backend must send CORS headers para uploads from cross-origin.

### File size limits
- Client-side: check en JS
- Server-side: check en backend + reject with 413

### File type validation
- Client: extension check (unreliable)
- Server: check actual MIME type (secure)

### Multiple files sequential vs parallel
- Sequential: safer, slower
- Parallel: faster, may overwhelm backend

## Post-upload
- Refresh list
- Show success toast
- Update related data (if attachments visible en detail)

## Offline scenarios
Apps que soportan offline:
- Field workers (technicians, delivery)
- Mobile users con conectividad intermitente
- Retail (POS con network flaky)

## Options

### 1. PWA (Progressive Web App)
Browser-based, limited offline capability.

### 2. Native mobile con MDK
Full offline con local DB (SQLite).

### 3. SAP Mobile Services
More complete offline framework.

## PWA approach

### Service worker
```javascript
// sw.js
self.addEventListener('install', (e) => {
    e.waitUntil(caches.open('v1').then((cache) => {
        return cache.addAll(['/index.html', '/resources/sap-ui-core.js', ...]);
    }));
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (e) => {
    e.respondWith(caches.match(e.request).then((cached) => {
        return cached || fetch(e.request);
    }));
});
```

Register in main:
```javascript
if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
    navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js');
}
```

### Manifest.webmanifest
```json
{
    'name': 'My Fiori App',
    'short_name': 'MyApp',
    'display': 'standalone',
    'start_url': '/',
    'icons': [{ 'src': '/logo.png', 'sizes': '512x512', 'type': 'image/png' }]
}
```

User can 'Add to home screen'.

### Data offline
Cache OData responses en IndexedDB:
```javascript
var oModel = new sap.ui.model.odata.v2.ODataModel(url, {
    disableHeadRequestForToken: true,
    persistTechnicalMessages: false
});

// Manually cache responses
var aCached = await oModel.read('/Products');
localforage.setItem('products', aCached);
```

## Sync patterns

### Optimistic
User makes changes offline → app assumes success → sync when online.

Conflict resolution needed if server has newer version.

### Pessimistic
Only show data when online. Fail gracefully if offline.

Simpler but less useful.

## Offline queue
```javascript
async function queueUpdate(entity, data) {
    if (navigator.onLine) {
        return await sendToServer(entity, data);
    } else {
        var queue = await localforage.getItem('offlineQueue') || [];
        queue.push({ entity, data, timestamp: Date.now() });
        await localforage.setItem('offlineQueue', queue);
        return { success: true, offline: true };
    }
}

// When online again
window.addEventListener('online', async () => {
    var queue = await localforage.getItem('offlineQueue') || [];
    for (var op of queue) {
        await sendToServer(op.entity, op.data);
    }
    await localforage.removeItem('offlineQueue');
});
```

## Conflict resolution
### Last-write-wins
Simple: whoever writes last wins.

### Merge
App logic combines changes intelligently.

### User-decides
Show both versions → user picks.

## Storage limits
- LocalStorage: 5-10 MB per origin (limited)
- IndexedDB: 50 MB+ typical, no hard limit browser-side
- Cache Storage: similar

## MDK offline
### SQLite local
- Structured local storage
- Query with SQL
- Compact vs JSON blobs

### Delta sync
- Server tracks changes since last sync
- Only send deltas (efficient over bandwidth)

### Conflict handling
- Timestamps or version numbers
- Sync engine resolves

## Common issues
- **Stale cache** — user sees old data
- **Storage full** — silent fail, app misbehaves
- **Sync conflicts** — data inconsistency

## Best practices
- **Small data first** — heavy data on demand
- **Version everything** — for conflict resolution
- **Show sync status** — user knows what's synced
- **Automatic retry** — con backoff
- **Storage monitoring** — alert if near limits

## Enfoques

### 1. Server-side (recomendado)
Backend genera PDF, app descarga.

Opciones backend:
- **Adobe Document Services** (SAP integrated)
- **SmartForms** (S/4HANA con Adobe forms output)
- **Custom** — Node.js con pdfkit, Puppeteer
- **Reports** en OData service

### 2. Client-side
Browser-based generation. Limited but no backend needed.

Libraries:
- **jsPDF** — simple PDFs
- **pdfmake** — con layouts
- **html2pdf.js** — HTML to PDF

## Server-side flow

### Backend API
```
GET /api/orders/12345/pdf
Headers: Accept: application/pdf
```

Returns binary PDF.

### Client
```javascript
var sUrl = '/api/orders/12345/pdf';
fetch(sUrl).then(res => res.blob()).then(blob => {
    var url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    window.open(url);
});
```

### O direct download
```javascript
var oLink = document.createElement('a');
oLink.href = sUrl;
oLink.download = 'order-12345.pdf';
oLink.click();
```

## Client-side jsPDF
```javascript
sap.ui.require(['thirdparty/jspdf'], function() {
    var doc = new jsPDF();
    doc.text('Order #12345', 10, 10);
    doc.text('Customer: ACME', 10, 20);
    doc.text('Total: $1,500.00', 10, 30);
    doc.save('order.pdf');
});
```

## Print current view (browser)
```javascript
window.print();
```

Uses browser's print dialog. User can 'Print to PDF'.

### CSS for print
```css
@media print {
    .no-print { display: none; }
    body { font-size: 12pt; }
}
```

Hide navigation/toolbar en impresión.

## Adobe Document Services (SAP)
Enterprise-grade PDF generation:
- Design forms en Adobe LiveCycle Designer
- Deploy to SAP
- Call service to render con data

### From Fiori
```javascript
var oRequest = {
    formName: 'ZFORM_ORDER',
    orderData: { ... }
};
fetch('/api/adobe/render', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify(oRequest),
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
}).then(r => r.blob()).then(pdfBlob => {
    var url = URL.createObjectURL(pdfBlob);
    window.open(url);
});
```

## Puppeteer server-side
```javascript
// Backend Node.js
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

app.get('/api/orders/:id/pdf', async (req, res) => {
    const browser = await puppeteer.launch();
    const page = await browser.newPage();
    await page.goto(`https://myapp/order/${req.params.id}?print=1`, { waitUntil: 'networkidle0' });
    const pdf = await page.pdf({ format: 'A4', printBackground: true });
    await browser.close();
    res.contentType('application/pdf');
    res.send(pdf);
});
```

Renders live page → PDF. Very flexible.

## Multi-page PDFs
Split long content:
```javascript
doc.addPage();  // jsPDF
doc.text('Page 2 content', 10, 10);
```

## Common issues
- **Fonts missing** — embed fonts if custom
- **Chart doesn't render** — server-side needs headless browser (Puppeteer)
- **File huge** — compress images before embedding
- **CORS** — client-side PDF creation, no CORS issue; server-side generation → CORS if cross-origin

## Best practices
- **Server-side** for consistent output
- **Cache** generated PDFs si repetidos
- **Async generation** para long docs (background job + notify)
- **Preview** antes de download (open PDF in tab)

## Locale-aware formatting
SAPUI5 auto-formatea basado en locale del user.

### Number
```javascript
var oNumberFormat = sap.ui.core.format.NumberFormat.getFloatInstance({
    minFractionDigits: 2,
    maxFractionDigits: 2
});
var sFormatted = oNumberFormat.format(1234.5);
// EN: '1,234.50'
// ES: '1.234,50'
// DE: '1.234,50'
```

### Currency
```javascript
var oCurrencyFormat = sap.ui.core.format.NumberFormat.getCurrencyInstance();
oCurrencyFormat.format(1500, 'USD');
// EN: '$1,500.00'
// ES: '1.500,00 US$'

oCurrencyFormat.format(1500, 'COP');
// ES-CO: '$ 1.500,00'
```

### Date
```javascript
var oDateFormat = sap.ui.core.format.DateFormat.getDateInstance({ style: 'medium' });
oDateFormat.format(new Date());
// EN: 'Jul 28, 2026'
// ES: '28 jul 2026'
// DE: '28.07.2026'
```

### DateTime
```javascript
var oFormat = sap.ui.core.format.DateFormat.getDateTimeInstance({
    style: 'medium'
});
oFormat.format(new Date());
```

### Custom pattern
```javascript
var oFormat = sap.ui.core.format.DateFormat.getDateInstance({ pattern: 'yyyy-MM-dd' });
oFormat.format(new Date());  // 2026-07-28
```

## Binding types con formatters
```xml
<Text text='{
    path: 'BirthDate',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Date',
    formatOptions: { style: 'medium' }
}'/>

<Text text='{
    path: 'Amount',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Currency',
    formatOptions: { showMeasure: true }
}'/>

<Text text='{
    path: 'Percentage',
    type: 'sap.ui.model.type.Float',
    formatOptions: { style: 'percent' }
}'/>
```

## Locale detection
SAPUI5 usa:
1. URL param `sap-ui-language=es`
2. Cookie/user preference
3. Browser Accept-Language
4. Default (en_US)

### Ver current
```javascript
sap.ui.getCore().getConfiguration().getLanguage();
// 'es' o 'es-CO' o 'de-DE' etc.
```

## Set language
```javascript
sap.ui.getCore().getConfiguration().setLanguage('es');
// May require app restart to fully apply
```

## Timezone handling
```javascript
var oDate = new Date();
var sFormatted = sap.ui.core.format.DateFormat.getDateTimeInstance().format(oDate);
// Uses user's local timezone

// Explicit timezone (SAPUI5 1.113+)
sap.ui.core.format.DateFormat.getDateTimeInstance({ ..., UTC: true });
```

## Number formatter groups
- **Float**: standard numbers
- **Integer**: whole numbers
- **Currency**: with currency symbol
- **Unit**: 5 kg, 100 km/h
- **Percent**: 45%

## Currency conversion
App calls service:
```javascript
var oRate = await fetch('/api/exchange/USD-COP').then(r => r.json());
var amountCOP = amountUSD * oRate.rate;
```

Display both:
```xml
<Text text='Monto original: $1,500.00 USD'/>
<Text text='En COP: {= ${Amount} * ${ExchangeRate} } COP'/>
```

## Right-to-left (RTL)
Arabic, Hebrew:
```javascript
sap.ui.getCore().getConfiguration().setRTL(true);
```

All UI mirrors.

## Common issues
- **Wrong currency symbol** — locale-specific rendering
- **Date parses incorrectly** — user enters DD/MM but locale expects MM/DD
- **Very small numbers** — scientific notation appears (`1.5e-3`), use pattern

## Best practices
- **Never hardcode** date formats
- **Server sends ISO 8601** dates (`2026-07-28T15:30:00Z`)
- **Client formats** per user locale
- **Test locales** — long translations may break layout

## CAP auth patterns

### Enable auth
```bash
cds add xsuaa
```

Genera manifest + xs-security.json.

### Roles + scopes
```json
// xs-security.json
{
    'xsappname': 'my-cap-app',
    'scopes': [
        { 'name': '$XSAPPNAME.User', 'description': 'General user' },
        { 'name': '$XSAPPNAME.Admin', 'description': 'Admin' },
        { 'name': '$XSAPPNAME.SalesRep', 'description': 'Sales rep' }
    ],
    'role-templates': [
        { 'name': 'User', 'scope-references': ['$XSAPPNAME.User'] },
        { 'name': 'Admin', 'scope-references': ['$XSAPPNAME.Admin'] },
        { 'name': 'SalesRep', 'scope-references': ['$XSAPPNAME.SalesRep'] }
    ]
}
```

## CDS annotations
### Service-level
```cds
service CatalogService @(requires: 'authenticated-user') {
    entity Products as projection on my.Products;
}
```

All users must be authenticated. Guests denied.

### Restrict entity
```cds
annotate CatalogService.Products with @(restrict: [
    { grant: 'READ', to: 'authenticated-user' },
    { grant: 'WRITE', to: 'Admin' },
    { grant: 'DELETE', to: 'Admin' }
]);
```

### Action-level
```cds
annotate CatalogService.Products with actions {
    approve @(requires: ['Admin', 'Manager']);
};
```

### Attribute-based access (multi-tenancy)
```cds
annotate CatalogService.Products with @(restrict: [
    { grant: 'READ', to: 'authenticated-user', where: 'tenant = $user.tenant' }
]);
```

User sees only their tenant's data.

## Runtime enforcement
CAP framework:
- Parses JWT for scopes + attributes
- Applies auth checks per request
- Rejects with 403 si insufficient

## User context
```javascript
srv.on('READ', 'Products', async (req) => {
    const user = req.user;
    console.log(user.id);         // user email
    console.log(user.roles);      // list of roles
    console.log(user.attr);       // custom attributes
});
```

## Draft admin
```cds
annotate CatalogService.Products with @(cds.persistence.skip);  // don't persist directly

service CatalogService {
    entity Products @(odata.draft.enabled) as projection on my.Products;
}
```

Draft mode restricts who can activate.

## Fiori launchpad integration
Assign role collections to users. Fiori tile visible only con role.

## Test auth
### Local dev con mock user
```bash
# .cdsrc.json
{
    'requires': {
        'auth': { 'kind': 'mocked' }
    }
}
```

Mock users con predefined roles. Test different scenarios.

### Production con XSUAA
Real auth flow.

## Debug 403 errors
1. Check JWT payload:
```javascript
console.log(req.user.roles);
```
2. Verify role collection assigned to user en BTP
3. Check annotation matches (`Admin` en annotation vs `User_Admin` en role — different!)

## Row-level security
CAP restricts based on user attributes:

### Employees only see their own records
```cds
annotate HRService.Employees with @(restrict: [
    { grant: 'READ', to: 'authenticated-user', where: 'ID = $user.employeeId' }
]);
```

### Managers see their team
```cds
annotate HRService.Employees with @(restrict: [
    { grant: 'READ', to: 'Manager', where: 'managerID = $user.employeeId' }
]);
```

## Field-level security
Hide fields based on role:
```cds
annotate Products with {
    cost @(restrict: [{ grant: 'READ', to: 'Admin' }]);
};
```

Others see product but not cost.

## Best practices
- **Least privilege** — grant minimum needed
- **Composite roles** in BTP for common personas
- **Test each role** — verify boundaries
- **Audit access** — log sensitive operations
